The attached image (Fig. 10) displays confocal microscopy images of skeletal muscle 24 hours after intramuscular injection, illustrating the local inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11. The top row, showing tissue injected with AF647-labeled Nano-11 and OVA, reveals significant infiltration of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages, MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, and 1A8+ neutrophils, with intracellular Nano-11 (red) visible within these cells (green). The bottom row, representing injection with soluble OVA only, shows minimal cellular infiltration. This demonstrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response and facilitates the in vivo uptake of adsorbed antigens by immune cells.